# The fake camera feed (ticket T-14) is a raw YUV4MPEG2 stream: a text header
# followed by uncompressed planes. Those planes contain 0x0A bytes as ordinary
# pixel values, so a checkout that applied any end-of-line conversion would
# corrupt the frames while leaving the file superficially intact — the harness
# would then decode garbage and the overlay gate would fail for a reason that
# has nothing to do with the app. Marking it binary also stops git trying to
# diff or merge a megabyte of pixels as text.
*.y4m binary
